Treasure Island development project construction regulations › Reporting concerns or complaints; Noise reduction

Info Page
Learn about noise, dust, and hazardous materials control programs on the island.
Find full contact information here for reporting concerns and complaints about development construction activity.
For all development construction contract agreements, the following noise reduction practices will be incorporated for the contractor’s implementation:
Provide enclosures and mufflers for stationary equipment, shroud or shield impact tools and install barriers around particularly noisy activities at the construction sites so that the line of sight between the construction activities and nearby sensitive receptor locations is blocked;
Use construction equipment with lower noise emission ratings whenever feasible, particularly for air compressors;
Provide sound-control devices on equipment no less effective than those provided by the manufacturer;
Locate stationary equipment, material stockpiles and vehicle staging areas as far as practicable from sensitive receptor locations;
Prohibit unnecessary idling of internal combustion engines;
Require applicable construction related vehicles and equipment to use designated truck routes to access the project sites;

Property inspection and repairs policy for BMR Resales › Repair policies

Damage that must be repaired include but is not limited to:
Violations under the San Francisco Building Code either through visual inspection or notice from the City;
Defects in electrical system, wiring, heating and air conditioning, insulation, plumbing, and functional condition of finishes.
Appearance of toxic substances (such as asbestos, lead, and/or mold);
Needed repair to appliances furnished to owner upon purchase of the property;
Holes and other defects (except for holes from picture hangers) in walls, ceilings, floors, doors, windows, screens, carpets, countertops and similar appurtenances; and
Repairs needed, as determined by MOHCD, to put the property into a good and clean condition, including without limitation cleaning and painting.
